        <!-- 4.6 — .cache -->
        <section class="cache" data-section="04 — Best practices">
          <span class="eyebrow">Context is expensive</span>
          <h2 class="h-set">
            <span class="h-line"><span>Discounts</span></span>
          </h2>
          <p class="cache-open-line">
            Copilot re-reads your <b>cached</b> context at a tenth of the price.
            <b>90% off, every turn.</b>
          </p>
          <p class="cache-open-line cache-auto-line">
            Let Copilot choose the model and it takes
            <b>another 10% off</b> the request.
          </p>

          <div class="cache-close-line">
            <p>
              Model &middot; reasoning effort &middot; context size<sup>*</sup>
              &middot; tools &mdash; choose them before you start, then leave
              them alone.
            </p>
            <p class="cache-fn">
              * a Copilot setting, not the model&rsquo;s window
            </p>
          </div>

          <ul class="cache-habits">
            <li>
              <b>Leave the model on Auto.</b> Small jobs go to <em>cheap</em>
              models, hard prompts still escalate.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Do not switch model or effort mid-session.</b> The switch
              <em>invalidates</em> your cache.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Keep your instruction file steady.</b> One character changes
              the prefix, and the cache is <em>invalidated</em>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>New task, new chat.</b> Don't re-read old turns. Better <em>focus</em>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Give narrow jobs to subagents.</b> They run on small models,
              <em>outside</em> your context.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

